# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: Other | Scene: TyrantPath1

translate pt strings:

    old "Do not listen to her!"
    new "Não a ouça!"

    old "Seize Marion Achillea immediately!"
    new "Prendam Marion Achillea imediatamente!"

    old "For a moment, there was confusion on the room, the soldiers unsure of whom to listen to."
    new "Por um momento, houve confusão na sala, com os soldados sem saber a quem ouvir."

    old "I am the king, and I order you to seize him!"
    new "Eu sou o rei, e ordeno que o prendam!"

    old "This reminder was enough for the soldiers, and they moved again, grabbing Marion, wrestling him to the ground as he tried to fight them."
    new "Este lembrete foi suficiente para os soldados, e eles se moveram novamente, agarrando Marion, lutando para imobilizá-lo no chão enquanto ele tentava resistir."

    old "You promised! Is your word worth nothing!?"
    new "Você prometeu! Sua palavra não vale nada!?"

    old "Marion's voice broke as he screamed. One of the soldiers cracked him across the mouth with his mailed fist."
    new "A voz de Marion quebrou enquanto ele gritava. Um dos soldados o atingiu na boca com o punho coberto de armadura."

    old "Blood and teeth splattered across the floor, and Marion slumped over. Either unconscious or too stunned to speak."
    new "Sangue e dentes espirraram pelo chão, e Marion desabou. Ou estava inconsciente, ou estava atordoado demais para falar."

    old "The soldiers began to drag him away."
    new "Os soldados começaram a arrastá-lo para longe."

    old "Thomas. I gave him my word he would be safe."
    new "Thomas. Eu lhe prometi que ele estaria seguro."

    old "And you were smart to lie to him like that, but I won't allow him to escape for what he did."
    new "E você foi esperta ao mentir para ele daquele jeito, mas não vou permitir que ele escape pelo que fez."

    old "He tried to destroy our country, kill me, and if he had won, he would have killed you too."
    new "Ele tentou destruir nosso país, me matar, e se tivesse vencido, também teria matado você."

    old "If we let him live in exile, it won't be long until he's back."
    new "Se o deixarmos viver no exílio, não vai demorar muito para que ele volte."

    old "Unlike father, I'm not going to let these problems fester. We rip the traitors out by the root, starting with Marion, the one who caused all of this."
    new "Diferente do meu pai, não vou deixar esses problemas se agravarem. Vamos arrancar os traidores pela raiz, começando por Marion, aquele que causou tudo isso."

    old "Sarah wanted to keep her word to Marion, but Thomas was right. He was the king, and his order stood over hers. There was nothing she could do."
    new "Sarah queria manter a palavra dada a Marion, mas Thomas estava certo. Ele era o rei, e a ordem dele se sobrepunha à dela. Não havia nada que ela pudesse fazer."

    old "Still, it did not trouble Sarah that much."
    new "Ainda assim, isso não incomodava tanto Sarah."

    old "Her brother had been right. Marion would have killed her without thinking anything of it."
    new "Seu irmão estava certo. Marion a teria matado sem pensar duas vezes."

    old "Whatever punishment was coming for him was entirely earned."
    new "Qualquer punição que estivesse por vir para ele era totalmente merecida."

    old "For now, this is where the game ends."
    new "Por enquanto, é aqui que o jogo termina."
